.nf
YASMV manual                                                 workspace

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
workspace open "<directory>"
workspace show

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Choose the directory used to store model revisions, named expressions, jobs,
traces, and scenarios. The default is .yasmv-workbench in the current directory.
Python 3.10 or newer is required.

open creates or opens the directory. Wait for active jobs to finish before
switching directories. A directory can have only one owner: close any other
CLI or HTTP service using it first.

show reports the directory, loaded native model, selected native trace, and
saved revision, job, and scenario selections.

Opening a workspace preserves the native model and trace selection. Use
read-model to load a model. The existing one-model-load-attempt rule applies;
start a new yasmv process to load another model.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> workspace open "./investigation"
>> workspace show

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help read-model, help goal, help property, help watch, help job, help scenario.
